{%- comment -%} Styles live in assets/ha-sections.css ("ABOUT THE CIRCLE, 30 SEPTEMBER"). {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — ABOUT THE CIRCLE 01: the opening and the envelope.
  Aloha's About The Circle artboard, 30 September 2026 (the page before a
  member signs in), with Ivan's build notes.

  The opening: HARTWICK ATELIER / BY PERSONAL INVITATION, THE CIRCLE, and her
  line on the right. Beneath it her envelopes (Aloha, 30 September, "The new
  envelope I've created for The Circle"): two wine envelopes photographed on
  a transparent ground, so they sit on the page's own ground and grain, and
  her gold wax seal with the House symbol on the front flap. The seal is a
  separate picture laid over the photograph (position, size and turn are
  settings, in % of the photograph) because it is the thing you press.
  The drawn Inkstone envelope and its small words are retired; her new
  design has no words on or around the envelopes. The label stays for
  screen readers and can be shown with `show_seal_text`.

  1 October 2026 (Aloha: "can you place this background and change the
  colours"): the opening sits on her grey paper (`paper`,
  HA_CIRCLE_HEADER_PAPER_GREY.jpg — light at the edges, darker under the
  envelopes), running up under the transparent menu like the other paper
  openings (header "Transparent on these pages" includes the-circle). THE
  CIRCLE and her line on the right are Chalk Blue, the line set as a pull
  line (Junicode SemiBold Italic); the two small labels stay ink.

  THE SEAL. Note 01: "The seal opens a letter in place; it is not an
  authentication gate." The letter belongs to the invitation form, whose
  updated design is still to come (Ivan, 30 September), so it is not built
  here. Until it is, the seal is a plain link down the page to "Within the
  Circle" (`seal_url`), so it never is a control that does nothing. When the letter is built, the seal becomes a real labelled button
  (note 05) that opens it in this same place.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign sid = section.id -%}

<section class="ha-section ha-cinv{% if section.settings.paper %} ha-cinv--paper{% endif %}"{% if section.settings.paper %} style="--ha-paper-bg: url({{ section.settings.paper | image_url: width: 2400 }});"{% endif %} aria-labelledby="HaCinvTitle-{{ sid }}">
  <div class="ha-cinv__wrap">
    <div class="ha-cinv__head">
      <div class="ha-cinv__head-main">
        {%- if section.settings.crumb != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-cinv__crumb ha-record">{{ section.settings.crumb }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <h1 id="HaCinvTitle-{{ sid }}" class="ha-cinv__title ha-narrate">{{ section.settings.title }}</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="ha-cinv__head-aside">
        {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-cinv__intro ha-narrate ha-pull">{{ section.settings.intro }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.meta != blank -%}
          <p class="ha-cinv__meta ha-label">{{ section.settings.meta }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ha-cinv__stage">
      {%- if section.settings.image -%}
        {{
          section.settings.image
          | image_url: width: 2200
          | image_tag:
            class: 'ha-cinv__img',
            loading: 'eager',
            fetchpriority: 'high',
            sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 79vw, 120vw',
            widths: '750, 1100, 1500, 2200',
            alt: section.settings.image_alt
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'ha-cinv__img ha-cinv__img--placeholder' }}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- liquid
        assign seal_w = section.settings.seal_w | divided_by: 10.0
        assign seal_style = '--ha-cinv-seal-x: ' | append: section.settings.seal_x | append: '%; --ha-cinv-seal-y: ' | append: section.settings.seal_y | append: '%; --ha-cinv-seal-w: ' | append: seal_w | append: '%; --ha-cinv-seal-turn: ' | append: section.settings.seal_turn | append: 'deg;'
      -%}
      <a class="ha-cinv__seal" href="{{ section.settings.seal_url | default: '#within-the-circle' }}" style="{{ seal_style }}">
        {%- if section.settings.seal_image -%}
          {{ section.settings.seal_image | image_url: width: 320 | image_tag: class: 'ha-cinv__seal-img', loading: 'eager', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 4vw, 12vw', widths: '120, 200, 320', alt: '' }}
        {%- endif -%}
        <span class="{% unless section.settings.show_seal_text %}visually-hidden{% else %}ha-cinv__seal-label ha-record{% endunless %}">{{ section.settings.seal_text }}</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HA — Circle: invitation",
  "tag": "div",
  "class": "ha-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Opening" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "crumb", "label": "Reference line", "default": "Hartwick Atelier / By personal invitation" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "default": "THE CIRCLE" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "intro", "label": "Line on the right", "default": "A private circle of collectors, connected through Angela and the pieces they choose to live with." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "meta", "label": "Label beneath it", "default": "Private accessories / Personal attention / Shared stories" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "paper", "label": "Paper photograph", "info": "Aloha's grey paper (1 October), under the whole opening and the transparent menu. Empty = the page ground." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "The envelopes" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photograph", "info": "Aloha's envelopes, 30 September: HA_CIRCLE_ENVELOPES.png (transparent, sits on the page ground)." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Photograph description", "default": "Two wine-coloured envelopes with grey linings, one sealed with the gold Hartwick seal" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "The seal", "info": "The seal is the link, placed over the front envelope's flap. Positions are % of the photograph." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "seal_image", "label": "Seal", "info": "HA_CIRCLE_SEAL.png" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "seal_x", "label": "Centre, across", "min": 15, "max": 60, "step": 0.5, "unit": "%", "default": 35.5 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "seal_y", "label": "Centre, down", "min": 25, "max": 70, "step": 0.5, "unit": "%", "default": 48 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "seal_w", "label": "Width (tenths of %)", "min": 20, "max": 120, "step": 1, "default": 39, "info": "39 = 3.9% of the photograph's width, as she placed it." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "seal_turn", "label": "Turn", "min": -30, "max": 30, "step": 1, "unit": "°", "default": 12 },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal_text", "label": "Seal label", "default": "Break the seal", "info": "Read out by screen readers; shown only when ticked below." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_seal_text", "label": "Show the label beneath the envelopes", "default": false },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal_url", "label": "Seal link", "default": "#within-the-circle", "info": "Until the letter is built the seal leads down the page. An anchor on this page or a link." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "HA — Circle: invitation" }]
}
{% endschema %}
